  "scope": "Rust accepted-party service/SQL/presentation ownership, authenticated HTTP and declared native/provider fixtures. No new original executable execution, actual played engine/world or deployed activation proof.",
  "reproduced_gap": {
    "trigger": "Four accepted physical connections each admit four local seats, filling sixteen player slots, then the authenticated leader asks for an activity link.",
    "before": "The actual Python endpoint returns200, advertises current_size4/max_size16 and issues a join secret.",
    "after": "Rust counts admitted local seats, commits activity-link revocation and returns409 for the full party. Releasing seats yields current_size13 and a fresh secret.",
    "red_report": "party-directory-red-report.json",
    "red_log": "party-directory-red-step-1.log",
    "boundary": "Activity-link publication/revocation is declared native service policy; the existing original privacy leaf remains separate."
  },
  "rust_authorities": "Rust now owns accepted party membership/invitations/leadership/privacy/activity, target and role gates, request quotas/replay, public party projections and transactional SQL. Native transactions bind the actual queue owner and invoke its sessions, queue, Ready/countdown and invalidation policies inside Rust. The actual sixteen-local-seat/four-connection activity mismatch is reproduced and corrected; full-party activity revocation commits before HTTP rejection. SQL-trigger failure rolls back membership/version/invites/replay; ordinary rejection does not mutate membership. Python retains typed HTTP/clock/SQLite/shared-provider/countdown IO. These are native service rules, not recovered Live procedures. Shared account/clan authentication and CRUD, general rate/readers, full Rust service replacement, cross-store recovery and original/native played/delivered gates remain open.",
  "checks": [
    "Authenticated party creation, invitation targets across legacy/friend/Discord/Steam/clan/member routes, target-bound acceptance/decline/block/cancel, leader/version gates and one-party membership",
    "Actual native local-seat capacity, committed full-party activity revocation, fresh-secret reissue, expiry/conditional refresh and concurrent acceptance",
    "Native action/body/UUID/secret validation and prior ASCII Unicode/surrogate-pair request canonicalization",
    "Bounded one-use SQL/provider/core continuations, expected change guards,1024-step/1MiB journal bounds and128 transaction-owner cap",
    "Private journal limit controls are distinct from authenticated HTTP and actual source-handle retirement checks",
    "Rust queue-owner handle binding, source retirement exclusion and native session/queue/Ready/countdown/effect callbacks",
    "Python privacy aliases cannot grant closed-party admission; actual SQLite trigger failure rolls back roster/version/invites/replay and retry commits once",
    "Nested directory reads preserve an outer transaction and its rollback",
    "Legacy and opt-in local-player/appearance/privacy/countdown/postgame projections preserve private identities and actual shared profile/provider facts",
    "Frozen full backend plus production ABI checks cover Steam/friends/voice/queue/consent/countdown/result integration; existing numerical original fixtures remain regression inputs"
  ],
